  "notes": [
    "Anchor is the first self-transfer (iUSDT); all v2 iTokens ran the same transfer logic. Campaign is every Transfer with from == to on the eleven bZx loan pools until the fix, plus each duplicator's burns that paid out; burns after the fix paid nothing and are left out.",
    "Loss nets each attacker's own deposits it minted before duplicating and later burned back out (rule 14). Self-transfers of 1 iBZRX by 0x81341399 after the fix gained nothing and are excluded; the iBZRX that 0x68cfbe33 duplicated could not be redeemed.",
    "This vulnerability differs from the February 2020 bZx incidents (0xb5c8bd94, 0x762881b0) and the December 2023 iYFI donation incident, which remain separate (rule 4)."
